       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg once daily. The usual range is 2.5 to 10 mg. A dose this high could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, peripheral edema, and shock. Your patient's kidney and liver function are normal and there are no allergies, so nothing here would justify it.\n\nThe 50 mg may be a typo. Here are some options:\n- **5 mg by mouth once daily**, the usual starting dose.\n- **10 mg by mouth once daily**, the maximum dose.\n- **2.5 mg by mouth once daily**, a lower starting dose, often used for frail patients or those on other antihypertensives.\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do mean 50 mg, tell me the clinical reason. I'd suggest confirming it with pharmacy first, and I can add a note to the order."
